0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, set in the two EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three. (asm80 wants the vector number: RST 1 = RST 08h.)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    RST 3  18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 6  30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block has no jumps inside itself, so it works at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   a held-back key;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_'
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   1-(1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0100   31 FC 08               LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103   C3 D8 05               JMP   start   ; In the checked generic build this is at 0000h
0106                             ;   (and `start` sets SP): its first byte, C3h,
0106                             ;   is what an undefined word runs into, as
0106                             ;   CP/M's own JMP at 0000h is in a .COM: e_hi.
0106                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              DB   0,0,0   ; 03  spare
0106                          ENDIF      
0106   CF           RDROP:    RST   1   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0107   DF                     RST   3   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
0108   2A 34 09     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
010B   5E                     MOV   E,M   
010C   23                     INX   H   
010D   56                     MOV   D,M   
010E   23                     INX   H   
010F   22 34 09               SHLD   RSP   
0112   EB                     XCHG      
0113   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0114   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0115   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
0118                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   
011D   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
011E   CF                     RST   1   
011F   F7                     RST   6   
0120                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBB   A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     MOV   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
0128                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 27 04               JMP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
012B                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
012B   CD 27 01     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
012E   E1                     POP   H   
012F   F7                     RST   6   
0130                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JMP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD 92 04               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LDAX   B   
0138   03                     INX   B   
0139   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   DA 7E 01               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013E   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
0140   DA 6E 01               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0143   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0145   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0147   DA 41 03               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
014A   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
014C   DA 6C 01               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014F   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
0151   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0153   DA AD 01               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0156   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
0158   DA 6A 01               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
015B   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
015D   DA A7 01               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0160   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
0162                          IF   CHECKED   
0162   CA 34 01               JZ   next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
0165   D2 DE 04               JNC   e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0168                          ENDIF      
0168                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0168                          ENDIF      
0168   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
016A   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
016C   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
016E                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
016E                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
016E   C6 21        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0170   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0171   16 03                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0173   FE 37                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0175   1A                     LDAX   D   
0176   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0177                          IFN   CPM   
                              MVI   A,0   
                              RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0177                          ENDIF      
0177                          IF   CPM   
0177   3E 01                  MVI   A,1   
0179   CE 00                  ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
017B                          ENDIF      
017B   57                     MOV   D,A   
017C   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
017D   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
017E                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
017E   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
0180   C2 34 01               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
0183   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0186                             ; =============================================================================
0186                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0186                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0186                             ; =============================================================================
0186   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0187   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0188   AA                     XRA   D   
0189   67                     MOV   H,A   
018A   7D                     MOV   A,L   
018B   AB                     XRA   E   
018C   6F                     MOV   L,A   
018D   F7                     RST   6   
018E   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
018F   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0190   B2                     ORA   D   
0191   67                     MOV   H,A   
0192   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0193   B3                     ORA   E   
0194   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0195   F7                     RST   6   
0196   E7           H_NOT:    RST   4   ; ~x = -x - 1
0197   2B                     DCX   H   
0198   F7                     RST   6   
0199                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0199                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0199   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
019A   2A 7C 09               LHLD   HEAP   
019D   E5                     PUSH   H   
019E   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
019F                          IF   CHECKED   
019F   CD 49 04               CALL   chkhp   
01A2                          ENDIF      
01A2   22 7C 09               SHLD   HEAP   
01A5   E1                     POP   H   
01A6   F7                     RST   6   
01A7                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
01A7                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01A7   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
01A8   87                     ADD   A   
01A9   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01AA   26 09                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
01AC   F7                     RST   6   
01AD                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01AD                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01AD   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
01AE   87                     ADD   A   
01AF   6F                     MOV   L,A   
01B0   26 09                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01B2   50                     MOV   D,B   
01B3   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
01B4   4E                     MOV   C,M   
01B5   23                     INX   H   
01B6   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
01B7                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
01B7                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
01B7                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
01B7                             ; the one that was used up.
01B7                RPUSHD:      
01B7                          IF   CHECKED   
01B7   CD C9 04               CALL   chkbrk   ; Ctrl-C is checked at every word call, block
01BA                          ENDIF      ;   entry, loop-back and "{"
01BA   2A 34 09               LHLD   RSP   
01BD   2B                     DCX   H   
01BE   72                     MOV   M,D   
01BF   2B                     DCX   H   
01C0   73                     MOV   M,E   
01C1   22 34 09               SHLD   RSP   
01C4   E1                     POP   H   
01C5   F7                     RST   6   
01C6                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01C6                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01C6                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01C6                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01C6                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01C6                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01C6                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01C6   CD 08 04     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01C9   D2 2B 01               JNC   exec   
01CC   87           HX1:      ADD   A   
01CD   87                     ADD   A   
01CE   87                     ADD   A   
01CF   87                     ADD   A   
01D0   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
01D1   CD 08 04               CALL   hexc   
01D4   D2 E0 01               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
01D7   B2                     ORA   D   
01D8   77                     MOV   M,A   
01D9   23                     INX   H   
01DA   CD 08 04               CALL   hexc   
01DD   DA CC 01               JC   hx1   
01E0   36 C9        HX2:      MVI   M,0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01E2   F7                     RST   6   
01E3                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E3                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E3                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E3                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E3                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E3                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
01E3                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
01E3   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
01E4   CF           RET2:     RST   1   
01E5   44                     MOV   B,H   
01E6   4D                     MOV   C,L   
01E7   DF                     RST   3   
01E8                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01E8                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01E8                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
01E8   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
01E9   B5                     ORA   L   
01EA   CA D5 02               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
01ED   CD B1 03               CALL   skip   
01F0   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F1   C2 E4 01               JNZ   ret2   
01F4   C3 06 01               JMP   rdrop   
01F7                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01F7                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01F7                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01F7                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01F7                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01F7   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
01F8   03                     INX   B   
01F9   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01FB   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01FC   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
01FE   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
0200   D2 10 02               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
0203   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0204   87                     ADD   A   
0205   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0206   16 09                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0208   79                     MOV   A,C   
0209   12                     STAX   D   
020A   1C                     INR   E   
020B   78                     MOV   A,B   
020C   12                     STAX   D   
020D   C3 19 02               JMP   skipnx   
0210                DEF2:        
0210                          IF   CHECKED   
0210   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0211   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
0213   C2 F8 04               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0216                          ENDIF      
0216   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0217   60                     MOV   H,B   
0218   69                     MOV   L,C   
0219                SKIPNX:      
0219                          IF   CHECKED   
0219   0B                     DCX   B   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
021A                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
021A   CD B1 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
021D   F7                     RST   6   
021E   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
021F   23                     INX   H   
0220   56                     MOV   D,M   
0221   EB                     XCHG      
0222   F7                     RST   6   
0223                             ; =============================================================================
0223                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0223                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
0223                             ;  tail may run past that page.
0223                             ; =============================================================================
0223                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
0223                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0223                             ; the matching ")".
0223   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
0224   B5                     ORA   L   
0225   E1                     POP   H   
0226   CA 1A 02               JZ   skipo   
0229   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
022A   50                     MOV   D,B   
022B   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
022C   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   
022F                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
022F                             ; drops it and carries on.
022F   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
0230   B5                     ORA   L   
0231   CA 06 01               JZ   rdrop   
0234   CF                     RST   1   ; pop the block start ...
0235   44                     MOV   B,H   
0236   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0237   EB                     XCHG      
0238   C3 B7 01               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
023B                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
023B                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
023B   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
023C   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
023E   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0240   DA 47 03               JC   negnum   
0243   E7                     RST   4   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0244   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0245   19                     DAD   D   
0246   F7                     RST   6   
0247   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
0248   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0249   A2                     ANA   D   
024A   67                     MOV   H,A   
024B   7D                     MOV   A,L   
024C   A3                     ANA   E   
024D   6F                     MOV   L,A   
024E   F7                     RST   6   
024F                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
024F                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
024F                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
024F                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
024F   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
0250   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
0251   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0252   95                     SUB   L   
0253   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0254   9C                     SBB   H   
0255   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0256   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0257   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0258   AA                     XRA   D   
0259   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
025A   9F                     SBB   A   
025B   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
025C   67                     MOV   H,A   
025D   6F                     MOV   L,A   
025E   F7                     RST   6   
025F   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
0260   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0261   AB                     XRA   E   
0262   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0263   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0264   AA                     XRA   D   
0265   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0266   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
0268   9F                     SBB   A   
0269   67                     MOV   H,A   
026A   6F                     MOV   L,A   
026B   F7                     RST   6   
026C                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
026C                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
026C   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
026D   C5                     PUSH   B   
026E   44                     MOV   B,H   
026F   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
0270   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
0273   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0274   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0275   1F                     RAR      
0276   47                     MOV   B,A   
0277   79                     MOV   A,C   
0278   1F                     RAR      
0279   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
027A   D2 7E 02               JNC   mul2   
027D   19                     DAD   D   
027E   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
027F   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
0280   EB                     XCHG      
0281   78                     MOV   A,B   
0282   B1                     ORA   C   
0283   C2 73 02               JNZ   mul1   
0286   C1                     POP   B   
0287   F7                     RST   6   
0288                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0288                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0288                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0288                             ; stops on it.
0288                H_DIV:       
0288                          IF   CHECKED   
0288   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0289   B5                     ORA   L   
028A   CA F5 04               JZ   e_zero   
028D                          ENDIF      
028D   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
028E   C5                     PUSH   B   
028F   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0290   B7                     ORA   A   
0291   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
0292   AC                     XRA   H   
0293   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0294   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0295   B7                     ORA   A   
0296   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
0299   EB                     XCHG      
029A   7C                     MOV   A,H   
029B   B7                     ORA   A   
029C   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
029F   CD 64 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
02A2   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A3   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
02A6   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
02A7   60                     MOV   H,B   
02A8   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
02A9   F1                     POP   PSW   
02AA   FC 20 01               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
02AD   C1                     POP   B   
02AE   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
02AF   F7                     RST   6   
02B0                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02B0   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
02B1   F7                     RST   6   
02B2   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
02B3   F7                     RST   6   
02B4                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02B4                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02B4                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02B4                          IF   CHECKED   
02B4   CD 35 04               CALL   chkst   
02B7                          ENDIF      
02B7   D1                     POP   D   
02B8   73                     MOV   M,E   
02B9   23                     INX   H   
02BA   72                     MOV   M,D   
02BB   DF                     RST   3   
02BC                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02BC                          IF   CHECKED   
02BC   CD 35 04               CALL   chkst   
02BF                          ENDIF      
02BF   D1                     POP   D   
02C0   73                     MOV   M,E   
02C1   DF                     RST   3   
02C2                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02C2                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02C2   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
02C3   60                     MOV   H,B   
02C4   69                     MOV   L,C   
02C5   CD F5 03               CALL   skipstr   
02C8                          IF   CHECKED   
02C8   B7                     ORA   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02C9   CA ED 04               JZ   e_quote   
02CC                          ENDIF      
02CC   F7                     RST   6   
02CD                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02CD                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02CD                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02CD                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JZ   h_drop   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JNZ   pr1   
                              MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              ANI   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   5   
                              JMP   h_print   
02CD                          ENDIF      
02CD                          IF   CHECKED   
02CD                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02CD                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
02CD                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
02CD   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   H   
02CE   CD 69 04               CALL   prstr   
02D1   D1                     POP   D   
02D2   DF                     RST   3   
02D3                          ENDIF      
02D3   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
02D4   EF                     RST   5   
02D5   DF           H_DROP:   RST   3   ; ";" is this one byte
02D6                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02D6   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   B   
02D7   CD 96 03               CALL   psgn   
02DA   C1                     POP   B   
02DB   DF                     RST   3   
02DC                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
02DC   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
02DD   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
02DF   F7                     RST   6   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02E0                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02E0                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02E0                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02E0                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02E0   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
02E1   B7                     ORA   A   
02E2   FA 00 03               JM   line   
02E5   1E 28        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02E7   CD 1B 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02EA   C2 FC 02               JNZ   kt3   
02ED   1D                     DCR   E   
02EE   C2 E7 02               JNZ   kt2   
02F1   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02F2   B5                     ORA   L   
02F3   CA E5 02               JZ   kt1   
02F6   2B                     DCX   H   
02F7   7C                     MOV   A,H   
02F8   B5                     ORA   L   
02F9   C2 E5 02               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02FC                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02FC                          ENDIF      
02FC   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
02FD   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
02FF   F7                     RST   6   
0300                          IF   CPM   
0300                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
0300                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
0300   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
0303   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
0304   9F                     SBB   A   
0305   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
0306   EE 7F                  XRI   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
0308   32 7E 09               STA   LBHDR   
030B   C5                     PUSH   B   
030C   11 7E 09               LXI   D,LBHDR   
030F   0E 0A                  MVI   C,10   
0311   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0314   C1                     POP   B   
0315   21 7F 09               LXI   H,LBHDR+1   
0318   7E                     MOV   A,M   ; the count typed (0-127)
0319   2C                     INR   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
031A   85                     ADD   L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
031B   6F                     MOV   L,A   
031C   36 0D                  MVI   M,13   
031E   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0320   F7                     RST   6   
0321                          ENDIF      
0321                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBB   A   
                              ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CMA      
                              MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LXI   H,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JZ   ln2   
                              CPI   13   
                              JZ   ln5   
                              CPI   8   
                              JZ   ln4   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              MOV   A,L   
                              CMP   D   
                              JZ   ln2   ; full
                              MOV   M,E   
                              INR   L   
                              MOV   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   5   
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JMP   ln2   
                    LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
                              MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
                              RST   6   
0321                          ENDIF      
0321                             ; =============================================================================
0321                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
0321                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0321                             ; =============================================================================
0321                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0321                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0321                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0321                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0321                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0321                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0321                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0321                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0321                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0321   B4           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
0322   C2                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
0323   D6                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
0324   CD                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
0325   B2                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0326   47                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
0327   D3                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0328   23                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0329   2F                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
032A   6C                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
032B   44                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
032C   DC                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
032D   3B                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
032E   BC                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
032F   88                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
0330   B0                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
0331   D5                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0332   50                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
0333   5F                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
0334   4F                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
0335   E0                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
0336   1E                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
0337   F7                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
0338   E8                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
0339   E3                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
033A   86                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
033B   99                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
033C   C6                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
033D   14                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
033E   8E                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
033F   1D                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
0340   96                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
0341                PTABEND:      
0341                             ; =============================================================================
0341                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
0341                             ; =============================================================================
0341                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
0341   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
0342   0B                     DCX   B   
0343   CD 4D 03               CALL   rdnum   
0346   F7                     RST   6   
0347                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
0347   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
0348   CD 4D 03               CALL   rdnum   
034B   E7                     RST   4   
034C   F7                     RST   6   
034D                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
034D                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
034D   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
0350   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
0351   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0353   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0355   D0                     RNC      
0356   03                     INX   B   
0357   54                     MOV   D,H   
0358   5D                     MOV   E,L   
0359   29                     DAD   H   
035A   29                     DAD   H   
035B   19                     DAD   D   
035C   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
035D   5F                     MOV   E,A   
035E   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
0360   19                     DAD   D   
0361   C3 50 03               JMP   rdn1   
0364                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
0364                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
0364                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
0364                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
0364                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0364   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
0367   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0368   EE 02                  XRI   2   
036A   B2                     ORA   D   
036B   C2 78 03               JNZ   udv0   
036E   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
036F   1F                     RAR      
0370   67                     MOV   H,A   
0371   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0372   1F                     RAR      
0373   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
0374   78                     MOV   A,B   
0375   17                     RAL      
0376   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0377   C9                     RET      
0378   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
037A   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
037B   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
037C   79                     MOV   A,C   
037D   17                     RAL      
037E   4F                     MOV   C,A   
037F   78                     MOV   A,B   
0380   17                     RAL      
0381   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
0382   79                     MOV   A,C   
0383   93                     SUB   E   
0384   78                     MOV   A,B   
0385   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
0386   DA 8E 03               JC   udv2   
0389   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
038A   79                     MOV   A,C   
038B   93                     SUB   E   
038C   4F                     MOV   C,A   
038D   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
038E   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
038F   3D                     DCR   A   
0390   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
0391   C2 7B 03               JNZ   udv1   
0394   F1                     POP   PSW   
0395   C9                     RET      
0396                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0396   7C           PSGN:     MOV   A,H   
0397   B7                     ORA   A   
0398   F2 9F 03               JP   pdec   
039B   3E 2D                  MVI   A,"-"   
039D   EF                     RST   5   
039E   E7                     RST   4   
039F                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
039F                             ; Uses BC.
039F   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LXI   D,10   
03A2   CD 64 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, C = the last digit
03A5   79                     MOV   A,C   
03A6   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03A7   7C                     MOV   A,H   
03A8   B5                     ORA   L   
03A9   C4 9F 03               CNZ   pdec   
03AC   F1                     POP   PSW   
03AD   C6 30                  ADI   "0"   
03AF   EF                     RST   5   
03B0   C9                     RET      
03B1                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
03B1                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
03B1                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
03B1                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
03B1                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
03B1                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
03B1                             ; 
03B1                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
03B1                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
03B1                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
03B1                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. The place where
03B1                             ; the skip started is kept on the stack, for the report.
03B1                SKIP:        
03B1                          IF   CHECKED   
03B1   C5                     PUSH   B   
03B2   0B                     DCX   B   
03B3   0A                     LDAX   B   
03B4   03                     INX   B   
03B5   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
03B6                          ENDIF      
03B6   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
03B8   14           SK3:      INR   D   ; an opener: one deeper
03B9   0A           SK1:      LDAX   B   
03BA                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INX   B   
                              ORA   A   
                              JZ   endprog   
03BA                          ENDIF      
03BA                          IF   CHECKED   
03BA   B7                     ORA   A   
03BB   CA E9 03               JZ   sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
03BE   03                     INX   B   
03BF                          ENDIF      
03BF   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03C1   CC F5 03               CZ   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
03C4   D6 28                  SUI   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
03C6   CA B8 03               JZ   sk3   
03C9   3D                     DCR   A   ; ")"
03CA   CA D7 03               JZ   sk4   
03CD   D6 32                  SUI   "["-")"   
03CF   CA B8 03               JZ   sk3   
03D2   FE 02                  CPI   "]"-"["   
03D4   C2 B9 03               JNZ   sk1   
03D7   15           SK4:      DCR   D   
03D8                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RZ      ; the closer at this level
                              JMP   sk1   
03D8                          ENDIF      
03D8                          IF   CHECKED   
03D8   C2 B9 03               JNZ   sk1   
03DB   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
03DC   AB                     XRA   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
03DD   E6 06                  ANI   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
03DF   FE 02                  CPI   2   ;   closer, and only then
03E1   7A                     MOV   A,D   
03E2   D1                     POP   D   ; (where the skip started)
03E3   C0                     RNZ      
03E4   42                     MOV   B,D   ; N. The place is the opener
03E5   4B                     MOV   C,E   
03E6   C3 F0 03               JMP   sk7   
03E9   7B           SK6:      MOV   A,E   ; the text ran out:
03EA   E6 04                  ANI   4   
03EC   C2 83 01               JNZ   endprog   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
03EF   C1                     POP   B   
03F0   3E 4E        SK7:      MVI   A,"N"   
03F2   C3 FB 04               JMP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
03F5                          ENDIF      
03F5                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
03F5                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
03F5                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INX   B   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
                              INX   B   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JZ   ss0   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JNZ   skipstr   
                              RET      
03F5                          ENDIF      
03F5                          IF   CHECKED   
03F5                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
03F5                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
03F5   0A           SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
03F6   B7                     ORA   A   
03F7   C8                     RZ      
03F8   03                     INX   B   
03F9   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03FB   C8                     RZ      
03FC   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
03FE   C2 F5 03               JNZ   skipstr   
0401   0A                     LDAX   B   ; the escaped character
0402   B7                     ORA   A   
0403   C8                     RZ      
0404   03                     INX   B   
0405   C3 F5 03               JMP   skipstr   
0408                          ENDIF      
0408                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
0408                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
0408                             ; return with the carry clear.
0408   0A           HEXC:     LDAX   B   
0409   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
040B   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
040D   DA 19 04               JC   hc1   
0410   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   
0412   D6 11                  SUI   11h   
0414   FE 06                  CPI   6   
0416   D0                     RNC      
0417   D6 F6                  SUI   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
0419   03           HC1:      INX   B   
041A   C9                     RET      
041B                             ; =============================================================================
041B                             ;  Console layer: getk returns a waiting key in A (zero flag clear), or
041B                             ;  A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc (RST 5) prints A.
041B                             ;  Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are the host's KEY and
041B                             ;  CONOUT routines themselves.
041B                             ; =============================================================================
041B                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:     EQU   KEY   ; the host's routine does the whole job
041B                          ENDIF      
041B                          IF   CHECKED   
041B   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a key held back by the break check goes
041C   21 36 09               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   first, and is taken out of the buffer
041F   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0420   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
0422   E1                     POP   H   
0423   B7                     ORA   A   
0424   C0                     RNZ      
0425                          ENDIF      
0425                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              JMP   KEY   
0425                          ENDIF      
0425                          IF   CPM*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:        
0425                          ENDIF      
0425                          IF   CPM   
0425   3E FF                  MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
0427                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
0427                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
0427   C5           PUTC:     PUSH   B   
0428   D5                     PUSH   D   
0429   E5                     PUSH   H   
042A   5F                     MOV   E,A   
042B   0E 06                  MVI   C,6   
042D   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0430   E1                     POP   H   
0431   D1                     POP   D   
0432   C1                     POP   B   
0433   B7                     ORA   A   ; (for getk)
0434   C9                     RET      
0435                          ENDIF      
0435                             ; =============================================================================
0435                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0435                             ; =============================================================================
0435                          IF   CHECKED   
0435                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0435                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0435                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0435                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0435                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0435                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0435                             ; Keeps HL and BC.
0435   23           CHKST:    INX   H   
0436   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0437   2B                     DCX   H   
0438   FE 09                  CPI   LETPAGE   
043A   DA 44 04               JC   e_store   
043D                          ENDIF      
043D                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              RC      
043D                          ENDIF      
043D                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
043D   5F                     MOV   E,A   
043E   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
0441   3D                     DCR   A   
0442   BB                     CMP   E   
0443   D0                     RNC      
0444                          ENDIF      
0444                          IF   CHECKED   
0444   3E 4F        E_STORE:   MVI   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0446   C3 FB 04               JMP   errp   
0449                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the count, the carry is from adding
0449                             ; it, and the old top is on the stack under the return address. Stop if the
0449                             ; new top is not below the limit page, or is below the program's end.
0449                CHKHP:       
0449                          ENDIF      
0449                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0449                             ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
0449                             ; range, so the add is tested too: growing must not carry, and
0449                             ; releasing must.
0449   7A                     MOV   A,D   
044A   1F                     RAR      ; the carry comes in above the count's sign:
044B   C6 40                  ADI   40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
044D   87                     ADD   A   
044E   DA 62 04               JC   e_heap   
0451   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   
0454   3D                     DCR   A   
0455   BC                     CMP   H   
0456   DA 62 04               JC   e_heap   
0459                          ENDIF      
0459                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              MOV   A,H   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              JNC   e_heap   
0459                          ENDIF      
0459                          IF   CHECKED   
0459   EB                     XCHG      
045A   E5                     PUSH   H   ; the count
045B   2A 38 09               LHLD   NPEND   
045E   19                     DAD   D   ; carry: at or above the program's end
045F   E1                     POP   H   
0460   EB                     XCHG      
0461   D8                     RC      
0462   EB           E_HEAP:   XCHG      ; put the count back in TOS for the report,
0463   D1                     POP   D   ;   and drop the return address and the old
0464   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   ;   top
0466   C3 FB 04               JMP   errp   
0469                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0469                             ; "$", and the error report's texts). A NUL first is an error: Q.
0469   7E           PRSTR:    MOV   A,M   
046A   23                     INX   H   
046B   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
046D   C8                     RZ      
046E   B7                     ORA   A   
046F   CA 7F 04               JZ   e_dollar   
0472   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
0474   C2 7B 04               JNZ   prs1   
0477   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0478   23                     INX   H   
0479   E6 BF                  ANI   0BFh   
047B   EF           PRS1:     RST   5   
047C   C3 69 04               JMP   prstr   
047F   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   D   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
0480   E1                     POP   H   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0481   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
0483   C3 FC 04               JMP   error   
0486                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
0486                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
0486   3E 0D        PNL:      MVI   A,13   
0488   EF                     RST   5   
0489   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
048B   EF                     RST   5   
048C   E3           PMSG:     XTHL      
048D   CD 69 04               CALL   prstr   
0490   E3                     XTHL      
0491   C9                     RET      
0492                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
0492                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
0492                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
0492                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
0492                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
0492                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile.
0492   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
0493   21 05 F7               LXI   H,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
0496   39                     DAD   SP   
0497   DA C1 04               JC   e_under   
049A   24                     INR   H   
049B   C2 BB 04               JNZ   e_over   
049E   2A 34 09               LHLD   RSP   ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
04A1   7C                     MOV   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
04A2   FE 07                  CPI   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
04A4   C2 B8 04               JNZ   e_rover   ;   page, in the guard band)
04A7   7D                     MOV   A,L   
04A8   FE E1                  CPI   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
04AA   D2 AF 04               JNC   e_runder   
04AD   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
04AE   C9                     RET      
04AF   21 E0 07     E_RUNDER:   LXI   H,RSTOP   ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
04B2   22 34 09               SHLD   RSP   
04B5   3E 72                  MVI   A,"r"   
04B7   21                     DB   21h   ; (LXI H hides the next entry; HL is free)
04B8   3E 52        E_ROVER:   MVI   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
04BA   21                     DB   21h   
04BB   3E 53        E_OVER:   MVI   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
04BD   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
04BE   C3 FB 04               JMP   errp   
04C1   31 FC 08     E_UNDER:   LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
04C4   3E 73                  MVI   A,"s"   
04C6   C3 FC 04               JMP   error   
04C9                             ; chkbrk: a waiting key is read now; Ctrl-C stops the program, anything
04C9                             ; else is held for the next "?". Keeps BC, DE, HL.
04C9   CD 1B 04     CHKBRK:   CALL   getk   
04CC   C8                     RZ      
04CD   FE 03                  CPI   3   
04CF   32 36 09               STA   KEYBUF   
04D2   C0                     RNZ      
04D3   AF                     XRA   A   
04D4   32 36 09               STA   KEYBUF   
04D7   D1                     POP   D   ; Ctrl-C. Drop the return address; the cell on
04D8   E1                     POP   H   ;   top of the stack is the TOS that rpushd
04D9   3E 42                  MVI   A,"B"   ;   was about to bring back
04DB   C3 FC 04               JMP   error   
04DE                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
04DE                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a JMP, C3h, in
04DE                             ; every build: if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of an undefined
04DE                             ; word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
04DE   04           E_HI:     INR   B   
04DF   05                     DCR   B   
04E0   C2 F2 04               JNZ   e_resv   
04E3   E5                     PUSH   H   
04E4   CF                     RST   1   
04E5   44                     MOV   B,H   
04E6   4D                     MOV   C,L   
04E7   E1                     POP   H   
04E8   3E 55                  MVI   A,"U"   
04EA   C3 FC 04               JMP   error   
04ED                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
04ED                             ; a 3-byte LXI D (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
04ED   44           E_QUOTE:   MOV   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
04EE   4D                     MOV   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
04EF   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
04F1   11                     DB   11h   
04F2   3E 58        E_RESV:   MVI   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
04F4   11                     DB   11h   
04F5   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   MVI   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
04F7   11                     DB   11h   
04F8   3E 57        E_BRACK:   MVI   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
04FA   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CPI hides the one byte of errp)
04FB                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
04FB   D1           ERRP:     POP   D   
04FC                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
04FC                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
04FC                             ; 
04FC                             ;   Err X @ line,col
04FC                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
04FC                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
04FC                             ;   Rtn n
04FC   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   H   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
04FD   5F                     MOV   E,A   
04FE   CD 86 04               CALL   pnl   
0501   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
0506   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0507   EF                     RST   5   
0508   CD 8C 04               CALL   pmsg   
050B   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
050F   0B                     DCX   B   ; BC = the place
0510                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
0510                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
0510                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
0510   21 80 09               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0513   11 00 00               LXI   D,0   
0516   78                     MOV   A,B   
0517   FE 0A                  CPI   PROG/256   
0519   DA 33 05               JC   er3   
051C   24                     INR   H   
051D   6B                     MOV   L,E   ; HL = PROG
051E   13           ER1:      INX   D   ; a new line starts at HL
051F   E5                     PUSH   H   
0520   7D           ER2:      MOV   A,L   
0521   91                     SUB   C   
0522   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0523   98                     SBB   B   
0524   D2 32 05               JNC   er2x   ; reached the place
0527   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0528   23                     INX   H   
0529   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
052B   C2 20 05               JNZ   er2   
052E   F1                     POP   PSW   
052F   C3 1E 05               JMP   er1   
0532   E1           ER2X:     POP   H   
0533   C5           ER3:      PUSH   B   
0534   E5                     PUSH   H   
0535   EB                     XCHG      
0536   CD 9F 03               CALL   pdec   ; the line
0539   3E 2C                  MVI   A,","   
053B   EF                     RST   5   
053C   D1                     POP   D   
053D   E1                     POP   H   
053E   E5                     PUSH   H   
053F   CD D1 05               CALL   sub16   
0542   23                     INX   H   
0543   CD 9F 03               CALL   pdec   ; the column
0546   CD 86 04               CALL   pnl   
0549   22                     DB   22h   
054A   E1                     POP   H   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
054B   06 10                  MVI   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
054D   7E           ER4:      MOV   A,M   
054E   23                     INX   H   
054F   B7                     ORA   A   
0550   CA 67 05               JZ   er5   
0553   FE 0D                  CPI   13   
0555   CA 67 05               JZ   er5   
0558   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
055A   CA 67 05               JZ   er5   
